diff --git a/features/editing.feature b/features/editing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6c271d7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/editing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+Feature: Editing
+  As a todo app user
+  I want to edit the text of a todo
+  So that I can correct mistakes without losing the item
+
+  Scenario: Editing saves on Enter
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title    | completed |
+    | Old text | false     |
+  When the user double-clicks the label of the first todo item
+  And the user sets the edit input of the first todo item to "New text"
+  And the user presses Enter in the edit input of the first todo item
+  Then the first todo item does not have class "editing"
+  And the first todo item's label reads "New text"
+  And the first todo item's stored "title" value is "New text"
+
+  Scenario: Editing saves on blur
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title    | completed |
+    | Old text | false     |
+  When the user double-clicks the label of the first todo item
+  And the user sets the edit input of the first todo item to "Blurred"
+  And the edit input of the first todo item loses focus
+  Then the first todo item does not have class "editing"
+  And the first todo item's label reads "Blurred"
+
+  Scenario: Editing discards changes on Escape
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title    | completed |
+    | Old text | false     |
+  When the user double-clicks the label of the first todo item
+  And the user sets the edit input of the first todo item to "Changed"
+  And the user presses Escape in the edit input of the first todo item
+  Then the first todo item does not have class "editing"
+  And the first todo item's label reads "Old text"
+
+  Scenario: Editing to empty destroys the todo
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title     | completed |
+    | Remove me | false     |
+  When the user double-clicks the label of the first todo item
+  And the user sets the edit input of the first todo item to "   "
+  And the user presses Enter in the edit input of the first todo item
+  Then ".todo-list" contains exactly 0 todo items
+
+  Scenario: Editing focuses the edit input
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title    | completed |
+    | Focus me | false     |
+  When the user double-clicks the label of the first todo item
+  Then the edit input of the first todo item is focused
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4404081
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+Feature: Persistence
+  As a todo app user
+  I want my todos to survive a page reload
+  So that I do not lose my list
+
+  Scenario: New todos persist to localStorage
+  Given the app is loaded
+  When the user types "Buy milk" into ".new-todo"
+  And the user presses Enter in ".new-todo"
+  Then localStorage "todos-vanillajs" contains 1 item
+  And the persisted item at index 0 has title "Buy milk"
+  And the persisted item at index 0 has completed false
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo persists to localStorage
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | Task  | false     |
+  When the user clicks the toggle of the first todo item
+  Then the persisted item at index 0 has completed true
+
+  @contract
+  Scenario: Persisted todo items conform to the todo item schema
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | Alpha | false     |
+    | Beta  | true      |
+  Then localStorage "todos-vanillajs" is a JSON array
+  And each item in localStorage "todos-vanillajs" conforms to the "todo item" schema in "scantlings/todos-localstorage.md"
+
+  Scenario: Editing state is not persisted
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | Task  | false     |
+  When the user double-clicks the label of the first todo item
+  Then the persisted item at index 0 has exactly the keys "id", "title", "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Todos are restored after a reload
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | Kept  | false     |
+  When the app is reloaded
+  Then ".todo-list" contains exactly 1 todo item
+  And the first todo item's label reads "Kept"
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6db0c84
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+Feature: Routing
+  As a todo app user
+  I want to filter my todos by status
+  So that I can focus on what is active or done
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all to-do items
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | A     | false     |
+    | B     | true      |
+  Then ".todo-list" contains exactly 2 todo items
+  And the ".filters a.selected" has href "#/"
+
+  Scenario: Active route hides completed todos
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | A     | false     |
+    | B     | true      |
+  When the user navigates to "#/active"
+  Then the todo item with label "A" is visible
+  And the todo item with label "B" is hidden
+  And the ".filters a.selected" has href "#/active"
+
+  Scenario: Completed route hides active todos
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | A     | false     |
+    | B     | true      |
+  When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+  Then the todo item with label "A" is hidden
+  And the todo item with label "B" is visible
+  And the ".filters a.selected" has href "#/completed"
+
+  Scenario: Checking a todo in the active filter hides it
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | A     | false     |
+    | B     | true      |
+  And the user navigates to "#/active"
+  When the user clicks the toggle of the todo item with label "A"
+  Then the todo item with label "A" is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Editing a todo in a filtered state updates its label
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | A     | false     |
+  And the user navigates to "#/active"
+  When the user double-clicks the label of the todo item with label "A"
+  And the user sets the edit input of the todo item with label "A" to "Renamed"
+  And the user presses Enter in the edit input of the todo item with label "A"
+  Then the todo item with label "Renamed" is visible
+
+  Scenario: Active filter is restored after a reload
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | A     | false     |
+    | B     | true      |
+  And the user navigates to "#/active"
+  When the app is reloaded
+  Then the ".filters a.selected" has href "#/active"
+  And the todo item with label "A" is visible
+  And the todo item with label "B" is hidden
diff --git a/features/todos.feature b/features/todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..949cbcf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,133 @@
+Feature: Todos
+  As a todo app user
+  I want to create, complete, and remove todo items
+  So that I can track what needs doing
+
+  Scenario: Empty state hides main and footer
+  Given the app is loaded
+  Then the element with id "main" is hidden
+  And the element with id "footer" is hidden
+
+  Scenario: New todo input is focused on load
+  Given the app is loaded
+  Then ".new-todo" is focused
+
+  Scenario: Creating a todo appends it and clears the input
+  Given the app is loaded
+  When the user types "Buy a unicorn" into ".new-todo"
+  And the user presses Enter in ".new-todo"
+  Then ".todo-list" contains exactly 1 todo item
+  And the first todo item's label reads "Buy a unicorn"
+  And the ".new-todo" input value is empty
+
+  Scenario: Blank whitespace-only new todo is ignored
+  Asserts the app trims and rejects empty input
+  Given the app is loaded
+  When the user types "   " into ".new-todo"
+  And the user presses Enter in ".new-todo"
+  Then ".todo-list" contains exactly 0 todo items
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo marks it completed
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title    | completed |
+    | Taste JS | false     |
+  When the user clicks the toggle of the first todo item
+  Then the first todo item has class "completed"
+  And the first todo item's stored "completed" value is true
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a label enters editing mode
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title    | completed |
+    | Taste JS | false     |
+  When the user double-clicks the label of the first todo item
+  Then the first todo item has class "editing"
+  And the first todo item's edit input value is "Taste JS"
+
+  Scenario: Clicking destroy removes the todo
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title    | completed |
+    | Taste JS | false     |
+  When the user clicks the destroy button of the first todo item
+  Then ".todo-list" contains exactly 0 todo items
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows one active item with singular label
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | Only  | false     |
+  Then the ".todo-count" reads "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows several active items with plural label
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | A     | false     |
+    | B     | false     |
+  Then the ".todo-count" reads "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows zero active items with plural label
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | A     | true      |
+  Then the ".todo-count" reads "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter number is wrapped in a strong element
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | A     | false     |
+  Then the ".todo-count strong" contains the text "1"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes only completed todos
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title  | completed |
+    | Active | false     |
+    | Done   | true      |
+  When the user clicks ".clear-completed"
+  Then ".todo-list" contains exactly 1 todo item
+  And the remaining todo item's label reads "Active"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden with no completed todos
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title  | completed |
+    | Active | false     |
+  Then ".clear-completed" is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete checks every todo
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | A     | false     |
+    | B     | false     |
+  When the user clicks "#toggle-all"
+  Then every todo item has class "completed"
+  And "#toggle-all" is checked
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete unchecks every todo
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | A     | true      |
+    | B     | true      |
+  When the user clicks "#toggle-all"
+  Then no todo item has class "completed"
+  And "#toggle-all" is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all reflects all single items checked
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | A     | false     |
+    | B     | false     |
+  When the user clicks the toggle of the first todo item
+  And the user clicks the toggle of the second todo item
+  Then "#toggle-all" is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all is unchecked when not all items are complete
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title | completed |
+    | A     | true      |
+    | B     | false     |
+  Then "#toggle-all" is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all clears after clear completed
+  Given the app has the following todos:
+    | title  | completed |
+    | Active | false     |
+    | Done   | true      |
+  When the user clicks ".clear-completed"
+  Then "#toggle-all" is not checked
diff --git a/scantlings/todos-localstorage.md b/scantlings/todos-localstorage.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c3c3d56
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scantlings/todos-localstorage.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Scantling: todos-vanillajs localStorage shape
+
+Mechanical shape of the TodoMVC persistence contract. The app stores the todo
+collection in `localStorage` under the key `todos-vanillajs`. The stored value
+is a JSON array. Every element conforms to the `todo item` schema. The app MUST
+NOT persist any field outside this shape, including an `editing` flag.
+
+## todo item
+
+```json
+{
+  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
+  "title": "todo item",
+  "type": "object",
+  "additionalProperties": false,
+  "required": ["id", "title", "completed"],
+  "properties": {
+    "id": { "type": ["integer", "string"] },
+    "title": { "type": "string" },
+    "completed": { "type": "boolean" }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+## todos-vanillajs value
+
+A JSON array whose elements each conform to the `todo item` schema above.
